1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,740
In this game you share one five hundred and twelve
kilobit line between a whole shop of customers.

2
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:10,006
On that line,
this demo would take about sixteen minutes to download.

3
00:00:12,256 --> 00:00:19,616
Brazilian LAN House 2003. Six beige PCs,
a foosball table, and a neighbourhood that wants to play.

4
00:00:19,866 --> 00:00:26,155
You run the tabs, the power and the machines,
and when a PC freezes, you fix it from the network monitor.

5
00:00:26,405 --> 00:00:31,779
The whole demo is a hundred and fifty-eight megabytes,
and it ships for Windows, Mac and Linux.

6
00:00:32,179 --> 00:00:34,811
Worth a dip if you remember
paying by the hour.

7
00:00:35,211 --> 00:00:38,809
That's Demo Dip.
A new Steam demo, every day.
